1
00:00:09,843 --> 00:00:11,219
<i>There are some people</i>

2
00:00:11,302 --> 00:00:15,932
<i>who see aging naturally</i>
<i>as nothing but humiliation.</i>

3
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:17,392
Confirming.

4
00:00:18,476 --> 00:00:22,939
<i>How much did this woman spend</i>
<i>only to end up with such a pathetic face?</i>

5
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:27,110
<i>A gold mine that's been fully exploited.</i>

6
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:30,280
<i>And yet,</i>

7
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:33,033
<i>they never seem to learn their lesson.</i>

8
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:37,078
<i>After multiple surgeries</i>
<i>in an attempt to stop the aging process,</i>

9
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:40,165
<i>and with a face</i>
<i>over-saturated with hyaluronic acid,</i>

10
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:43,209
<i>this patient can</i>
<i>no longer smile naturally.</i>

11
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:46,629
Ms. Anna, we will
bring your smile back, I promise.

12
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:48,298
I know you will. I have faith.

13
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:50,175
You'll feel a little prick.

14
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:52,093
There.

15
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:54,054
<i>Still hoping to regain her smile,</i>

16
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:55,930
<i>she made the shocking decision</i>

17
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:58,391
<i>to go under the knife yet again.</i>

18
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:01,478
<i>How insecure can she be?</i>

19
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:03,980
You gotta check out this new club.

20
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:05,523
Who's that?

21
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:06,900
Isn't she super cute?

22
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:09,569
- Huh? I don't know.
- Good morning.

23
00:01:09,652 --> 00:01:11,654
<i>Out of all living creatures,</i>

24
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:15,408
<i>only humans try to defy</i>
<i>the laws of nature.</i>

25
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:16,326
Hina.

26
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:21,206
Tanaka, oh my…

27
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:22,415
No way.

28
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:24,292
I mean, my goodness!

29
00:01:25,376 --> 00:01:29,297
It's like I'm looking right at Nastassia!

30
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:31,925
Wow.

31
00:01:32,509 --> 00:01:34,135
You look so great!

32
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:40,266
<i>Fighting your natural appearance,</i>

33
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:42,352
<i>refusing to age…</i>

34
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:44,187
<i>What is there to gain from that?</i>

35
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:46,439
- Gauze.
- Here.

36
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:52,946
Suction, please.

37
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:55,907
<i>No matter how hard</i>
<i>you fight against nature,</i>

38
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:58,243
<i>you pay a price, one way or another.</i>

39
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:00,537
Enough already.

40
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:03,289
Those guys are totally staring at you.

41
00:02:07,001 --> 00:02:09,087
Don't worry about it.

42
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:10,880
Hey, guess what?

43
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:12,590
VOICE ACTOR AUDITIONS

44
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:14,634
I signed up.

45
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:16,594
Sorry, but you missed the cut-off.

46
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:19,055
He said he'd make an exception for me.

47
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:22,725
Oh wow, that's excellent!

48
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:27,021
Can I ask a favor?

49
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:30,150
You think you could give me
a little dance lesson?

50
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:33,111
The debt payments have all been processed.

51
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:35,697
However, since her father's debts were

52
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,533
accrued with an illegal lender,

53
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:42,954
we took all the necessary measures
to conceal our involvement.

54
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:47,167
Is she even planning
to show up to work today?

55
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,168
Oh.

56
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:52,297
I believe she's coming in
for Dr. Rui's surgery this morning.

57
00:02:52,797 --> 00:02:55,300
Surgery on her first day?

58
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:57,635
She said she would like to sit in on it.

59
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:03,600
- Excuse me? Doctor?
- Hm?

60
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:06,227
I noticed the way
you're using your scalpel.

61
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:09,939
Um, the superior labial artery…

62
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:12,192
- Take over.
- Yes, Doctor.

63
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:13,359
Suction.

64
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:15,862
- Tanuma, come with me.
- Okay.

65
00:03:22,202 --> 00:03:24,871
- Do you have something to say?
- Sorry.

66
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:27,749
It's just that you handled the scalpel

67
00:03:27,832 --> 00:03:30,001
in a way that could nick the artery.

68
00:03:30,084 --> 00:03:33,379
Do you know how many surgeries
our clinic does in a year?

69
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:37,175
Way more than any
third-rate teaching hospital.

70
00:03:38,509 --> 00:03:41,429
Is a doctor's skill measured
by the number of surgeries they do?

71
00:03:41,512 --> 00:03:43,139
What was that?

72
00:03:43,223 --> 00:03:46,142
So you're saying,
no matter how much experience you have,

73
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,936
a surgeon can never improve?

74
00:03:48,019 --> 00:03:49,229
Director.

75
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:50,813
Hm.

76
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:53,149
If that's what you're saying,

77
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:55,860
why don't we have you perform the surgery?

78
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:57,362
What?

79
00:03:57,445 --> 00:04:00,782
I think we're all curious
to see if you're capable.

80
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:05,662
No, I won't.

81
00:04:06,454 --> 00:04:07,580
And why not?

82
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:10,750
Because I'm a doctor.

83
00:04:12,001 --> 00:04:14,170
I won't operate on someone who isn't sick.

84
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:24,639
Mm.

85
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:29,602
I'm relieved that's how you feel.

86
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,272
Dr. Numata,

87
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:34,482
we're glad to have you here.

88
00:04:34,565 --> 00:04:36,192
I think you'll fit in very well.

89
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:38,945
What does that mean?

90
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:46,244
In our world…

91
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:50,456
everyone we treat is sick.

92
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,028
CLINIC VICE-DIRECTOR
RUI KOMIYA

93
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:12,914
Sorry for the delay.

94
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:15,583
- It's no problem.
- So, what do you think?

95
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:18,002
I feel like I'm in Kabukicho.

96
00:06:19,295 --> 00:06:21,255
We sure aren't here to entertain guests.

97
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:26,135
Anyway, just to fill you in,
we've got three clinics in Tokyo.

98
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:30,181
Our flagship clinic in Roppongi,
one in Shinjuku, and one in Shibuya.

99
00:06:30,264 --> 00:06:33,309
The main clinic is Roppongi
is just the director and me.

100
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:36,854
In other words, I'm one of the best
cosmetic surgeons ever.

101
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:38,815
But, Tanuma, pretty soon--

102
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:41,734
Are you doing this on purpose?
My name is Numata.

103
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:44,362
I don't really care what your name is.

104
00:06:46,989 --> 00:06:47,865
Here.

105
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,243
- Take off your mask.
- What?

106
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:52,578
There are no clients here. Do it.

107
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:57,083
Take a look.

108
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:01,546
You look like you're pissed off
at the whole world.

109
00:07:01,629 --> 00:07:03,256
Patients don't want to see that.

110
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:06,134
First, just take a breath.

111
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:12,223
Relax the spot between your eyebrows.

112
00:07:15,017 --> 00:07:16,853
Better. And now,

113
00:07:17,353 --> 00:07:19,272
lift up the corners of your mouth.

114
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:25,820
LIFT THOSE LIPS

115
00:07:29,323 --> 00:07:31,993
All right, we'll work on it. Let's go.

116
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:33,244
Yes, understood.

117
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:34,996
- Hello.
- Oh, hello.

118
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:37,331
So this is the medical office.

119
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:41,627
- Just like a teaching hospital, right?
- No. It's completely different.

120
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:43,004
Hm?

121
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:46,215
Well, I'm guessing
you didn't have sales quotas.

122
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:50,011
But on the bright side,
the pay is unlike anything else.

123
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:54,307
They're all such money-grubbers.

124
00:07:55,224 --> 00:07:59,604
I mean, professional doctors are supposed
to be above material things like that,

125
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:00,813
aren't they?

126
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:01,814
Don't you agree?

127
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:05,776
It's your own fault for expecting ethics
from a plastic surgery clinic.

128
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:08,905
They hire their doctors
straight out of school.

129
00:08:09,405 --> 00:08:13,493
No residencies, no internships, and yet
they let them do high-risk surgeries,

130
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:15,620
paid for by insurance,
with zero experience.

131
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:19,248
That doesn't mean
they're not still good doctors though.

132
00:08:19,749 --> 00:08:20,791
Get this.

133
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:24,629
Their reviews are all way too positive
to be real.

134
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:26,172
<i>They gotta be paid for.</i>

135
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:30,593
This is our media PR department.
They control our online presence.

136
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:32,178
Normally, a third party would do it,

137
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:34,764
but the director insists
that it be done internally.

138
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:37,141
The internet is still a wild west.

139
00:08:37,725 --> 00:08:40,811
It just takes one keyboard warrior
to destroy your reputation.

140
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:43,064
Was that directed at me?

141
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:46,025
They hire people
to flood their page with positive reviews.

142
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:49,237
If there's anything negative,
they rush to have it taken down.

143
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,906
Honestly, it's not that different
from what the mob does.

144
00:08:52,698 --> 00:08:57,537
Honestly, I'm just surprised
that you're so surprised, Dr. Numata.

145
00:08:58,454 --> 00:09:00,248
What?

146
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:03,459
And here is our production department.

147
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:06,546
They handle everything video-related.
Subtitles, editing…

148
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:14,971
<i>This is the</i>
<i>"Name 100 Cosmetic Procedures" challenge!</i>

149
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:18,808
Our Head Nurse, Ms. Todoroki.

150
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:23,187
If you're confused about anything,
she'll help you out.

151
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:27,108
Feel free to ask anything.

152
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:30,319
And that includes anything on Dr. Rui.

153
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:33,447
I know everything from his income
to who he's slept with.

154
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:34,740
Uh-oh.

155
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:37,618
All jokes aside, though,

156
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:41,539
we've been following
the backlash you've been facing online.

157
00:09:41,622 --> 00:09:45,459
We were saying how tough it must be
to see your character dragged like that.

158
00:09:46,627 --> 00:09:48,754
While you're here, us on the nursing team

159
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:51,382
will do everything we possibly can

160
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:53,426
to help you feel comfortable,

161
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:55,511
and forget about that mess.

162
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:57,972
Oh. Thank you very much.

163
00:09:58,055 --> 00:10:00,224
- I look forward to working together.
- Mm.

164
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:03,019
- What did you think of her?
- Oh, her?

165
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:04,312
I thought she was nice.

166
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:07,023
I'm a bit relieved.
I was feeling like a fish out of water.

167
00:10:07,106 --> 00:10:12,028
Hm. You should know, Ms. Todoroki was
very close to Kanabun before her death.

168
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:13,821
Even outside of the office.

169
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:17,074
What? You're only telling me this now?

170
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:19,160
Wow, what are the odds

171
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:21,287
we end up with Dr. Backlash?

172
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:24,707
But she's gotta be good, right? I don't
think she would have been hired otherwise.

173
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:27,835
- Mm.
- She won't last long here anyway.

174
00:10:30,087 --> 00:10:31,505
Because I won't let her.

175
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:38,679
Through here is the VIP section. A special
area hidden from the general public.

176
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:43,851
It's like a ninja house.

177
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:48,814
Celebrities, politicians,
anyone high profile,

178
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:51,609
can enter through here
without being seen out front.

179
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:56,364
Hey, Mr. Hikita.
No employees allowed back here.

180
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:02,536
He's also one of our doctors.
We refer to him as Mr. Spot Remover.

181
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:04,121
Spot Remover?

182
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:09,126
Wait. I… I didn't see his name out front.

183
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:12,838
Mm. You wouldn't.
He's actually on the dark side.

184
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,173
The dark side?

185
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:16,592
No online presence.

186
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:21,263
No interaction with patients. He just
scrubs in and scrubs out. That's it.

187
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:25,810
What kind of cosmetic surgeon
doesn't use social media? Unreal.

188
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:30,106
He can't understand that not
all doctors want to be on social media.

189
00:11:30,189 --> 00:11:33,442
Says they're on "the dark side,"
like they're villains.

190
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:36,570
The whole thing is so discouraging.

191
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:40,533
If you hate it that much,

192
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:43,244
then why did you even agree to work there?

193
00:11:45,037 --> 00:11:46,288
Is the money that good?

194
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:50,501
That's part of it.

195
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:52,044
But

196
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:55,339
it's absolutely clear as day,

197
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:58,801
they're responsible for Kanabun's death,
and I'm gonna prove it.

198
00:11:58,884 --> 00:12:01,679
Whoa. You're gonna be a whistleblower.

199
00:12:02,304 --> 00:12:04,306
Not exactly.

200
00:12:04,807 --> 00:12:06,642
Hey, why do you always have sunglasses on?

201
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:07,852
Uh…

202
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:10,646
I mean, does it matter if I see your face?

203
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:12,857
Well, the thing is,

204
00:12:13,357 --> 00:12:15,067
I'm actually still healing.

205
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:34,587
Are you okay?

206
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:36,672
I can't anymore.

207
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:39,133
This song's too hard. I can't.

208
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:42,428
No, come on. You totally had it!

209
00:12:44,221 --> 00:12:46,682
Why didn't I ever train seriously
as a dancer?

210
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,518
Be kind to yourself.

211
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:52,271
You've got an amazing voice.

212
00:12:52,354 --> 00:12:55,775
That alone is good enough
to get you all the way. Right?

213
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:57,234
Nice job.

214
00:12:58,402 --> 00:13:00,571
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

215
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,407
- Ms. Tanaka, may I have a word?
- Yeah.

216
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:07,161
I was looking over your résumé
for the audition.

217
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:10,581
- Are you… using a stage name?
- Oh.

218
00:13:10,664 --> 00:13:12,249
- Stage name?
- Uh…

219
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:15,336
Mashiro Himenoki. Oh!

220
00:13:15,419 --> 00:13:18,130
- Great choice!
- Oh, thank you!

221
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:21,467
"Yoshiko Tanaka" just felt
plain and boring, you know?

222
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:23,844
I thought… Am I allowed to?

223
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:27,807
Hm. This is a first.
I've not seen many students do this.

224
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:31,268
But it's clear
you're taking this seriously, so

225
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:32,728
sure, it's fine.

226
00:13:32,812 --> 00:13:34,271
Thank you so much.

227
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:36,440
Well, in that case,
I should choose one too.

228
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:38,609
Your real name
is already a movie star name!

229
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,332
Oh! Fumi's here!

230
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:55,668
Uh, why did you order sushi?

231
00:13:55,751 --> 00:13:59,129
We told the regulars
that all our debt was paid off,

232
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:00,756
and they insisted on celebrating.

233
00:14:01,841 --> 00:14:03,384
Have a bite, Fumi.

234
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:04,718
- Oh.
- This is the good stuff.

235
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:06,178
- Oh my.
- It's expensive.

236
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:08,889
Of course, naturally.

237
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:10,766
- Damn straight.
- Fumi.

238
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,977
We'd like to thank you, your mother and I.

239
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:15,855
As a father,

240
00:14:16,355 --> 00:14:17,773
I'm so honored

241
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:20,234
to have a daughter like you, honey.

242
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:23,529
- Thanks a lot.
- That's so sweet.

243
00:14:24,029 --> 00:14:27,783
- I'm gonna cry.
- Stop it, or you'll make me cry too.

244
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:32,121
- All right.
- Listen up, everyone.

245
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:33,706
Thanks to Fumi here,

246
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:37,543
we've all been given
a second lease on life!

247
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:39,503
Everyone, drink!

248
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:49,430
Fumi, come on.
Come have one drink with us at least.

249
00:14:49,513 --> 00:14:50,806
Not now. I'm tired.

250
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:53,642
Wait, Mom,
you're not drinking alcohol, are you?

251
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:56,687
What about your cirrhosis?
That could be fatal.

252
00:14:56,770 --> 00:14:58,606
I'm drinking tea, okay? Lay off.

253
00:14:58,689 --> 00:15:00,399
- Oh, really?
- That's right.

254
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,569
Hey, make sure
Takashi understands the full story.

255
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:04,737
The debt isn't gone.

256
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,906
It was taken over by someone else.

257
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:10,242
Oh yeah, so who took over the debt anyway?

258
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:12,995
- What?
- Who took over the debt?

259
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:14,997
I'm your mother. I deserve to know.

260
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:18,167
We should bring them a gift or something
to thank for their generosity.

261
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:19,835
No. Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.

262
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,170
- Whoa, what?
- Uh…

263
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:24,256
A senior doctor in private practice,
he took it over.

264
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:27,217
But he doesn't want any fuss made.
He wants to stay anonymous.

265
00:15:27,801 --> 00:15:31,347
It's not like you were ever that much
of a mother before, so why start now?

266
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,059
Hey. Where's Takeru?

267
00:15:36,393 --> 00:15:40,230
Oh, him. He doesn't seem
to want to come out of his room at all.

268
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:42,483
Honestly, both you and Takeru,

269
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:44,652
you two can be so antisocial.

270
00:15:44,735 --> 00:15:46,111
Wow, really?

271
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:48,113
- Come out when you're ready.
- What?

272
00:15:54,119 --> 00:15:56,413
FUMI NUMATA HAS BEEN ARRESTED, RIGHT?

273
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:57,831
SEEING HER NAME MAKES ME SICK

274
00:15:57,915 --> 00:16:00,960
JUST SEEING HER NAME MAKES ME SICK

275
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:06,298
Takeru?

276
00:16:09,176 --> 00:16:10,260
Takeru.

277
00:16:11,428 --> 00:16:12,388
What's wrong?

278
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:15,849
You okay?

279
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:18,727
There's sushi downstairs.

280
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:21,563
I'm not hungry.

281
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:23,440
What is it?

282
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,609
What's going on?

283
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:30,406
I came here to see your charming face.
Show me that smile.

284
00:16:30,906 --> 00:16:33,033
How am I supposed to smile right now?

285
00:16:33,617 --> 00:16:35,995
Mm, you know what they say.

286
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:38,998
How when you smile,
it can make you happier, or whatever.

287
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:42,668
Look.

288
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:47,715
You look like you're pissed off
at the whole world.

289
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:52,344
Whatever.
Smiling isn't gonna help anything.

290
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:54,054
Yeah.

291
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:59,101
Well, I'm gonna go take a shower.

292
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:03,147
You're telling the truth?

293
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:05,983
Hm?

294
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:10,195
About Kanabun.

295
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,748
I did everything in my power as a doctor.

296
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:24,334
Okay.

297
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:36,764
- First, cleanse.
- All right.

298
00:17:37,806 --> 00:17:39,600
- Next, we'll suture.
- All right.

299
00:17:39,683 --> 00:17:42,269
Wait. The silicone.
She asked us to put it back.

300
00:17:42,352 --> 00:17:46,190
What? What's the point?
That tumor's gonna have to come out.

301
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:48,817
Okay, suturing now.

302
00:18:22,726 --> 00:18:25,229
<i>The director will be in the clinic</i>
<i>all day today.</i>

303
00:18:25,312 --> 00:18:28,649
We have several procedures on the books,
so I'll be assisting.

304
00:18:29,316 --> 00:18:32,444
Dr. Takada and Dr. Hamada from Shinjuku
will offer their support

305
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,279
with first-time and returning patients.

306
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:35,239
- Yes.
- Yes.

307
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:38,534
Numata, you'll be assisting them.

308
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:40,202
- Okay.
- Also--

309
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:41,245
I think…

310
00:18:43,455 --> 00:18:45,707
Numata will assist me
on the surgery today.

311
00:18:52,589 --> 00:18:53,715
What?

312
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:57,553
Dr. Rui, you have patients who will
require your time, so this works out.

313
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,942
All this in one day?

314
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:15,028
The director is often away
doing TV interviews and lectures,

315
00:19:15,112 --> 00:19:18,740
so they squeeze in as much as possible
on the days she's here.

316
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:25,747
Scalpel.

317
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:30,836
- Let's lift the right side a little.
- All right.

318
00:19:33,213 --> 00:19:35,132
I knew it. You are good.

319
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:37,092
Right. Next.

320
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:39,595
Are we cutting
the orbicularis oris muscle?

321
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:41,597
- Precisely.
- Okay.

322
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:44,850
Seeing as there is space
to work with on your face overall,

323
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:47,436
I suggest that the first thing we do

324
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:51,690
is smooth out this section
on your nasal bridge with hyaluronic acid.

325
00:19:51,773 --> 00:19:54,693
It should give you much better balance.

326
00:19:54,776 --> 00:19:58,197
I can also see that you have
dark circles under your eyes.

327
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,282
Let's add some volume there,
which will brighten…

328
00:20:00,365 --> 00:20:02,075
Okay, next.

329
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:15,923
Uh, are you doing
my liposuction correctly?

330
00:20:16,506 --> 00:20:18,759
Of course. Yes.

331
00:20:22,846 --> 00:20:23,931
Dr. Numata,

332
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:27,351
we have a procedure that requires
full anesthesia this afternoon,

333
00:20:27,434 --> 00:20:29,895
so make sure
to be back from lunch by 12:30.

334
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:31,355
That's only ten minutes!

335
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:52,793
Good, huh?

336
00:20:52,876 --> 00:20:54,086
What, my cigarette?

337
00:20:54,169 --> 00:20:56,713
Not that. I'm talking about her surgeries.

338
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:58,090
What?

339
00:20:58,757 --> 00:21:02,052
I've watched a lot of her surgeries,
and I still find it amazing.

340
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:04,304
I guess it's in her genes.

341
00:21:04,388 --> 00:21:08,100
That woman's earned her reputation
as The Hand of God.

342
00:21:08,183 --> 00:21:12,396
Yeah, but surely there are other doctors
just as gifted as she is, right?

343
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:14,982
- Dr. Tanuma--
- Numata.

344
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,608
Oh.

345
00:21:16,692 --> 00:21:21,446
I'm… I'm sure you probably
feel like a hypocrite working here,

346
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:25,033
but… but just know,
you keep your head down,

347
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:27,411
do as you're told,
you can become obscenely rich.

348
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:30,080
Just go with the flow.
Don't question things.

349
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:41,341
"Dark side." Yeah, right.

350
00:21:44,594 --> 00:21:45,846
Are you all right?

351
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:49,850
I'm a doctor. Can I take a look at you?

352
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,768
Here, let me see.

353
00:21:54,438 --> 00:21:56,815
Take deep breaths.
Just rest here for a moment.

354
00:21:56,898 --> 00:21:59,776
I… I'm fine. I just need to get a taxi.

355
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:02,446
- No, just sit here for a bit.
- I'm fine. Thank you.

356
00:22:02,529 --> 00:22:03,947
Taxi. I need to get a taxi.

357
00:22:04,031 --> 00:22:05,949
- Don't go.
- Yes. Thank you.

358
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:07,117
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

359
00:22:28,221 --> 00:22:29,222
Dr. Numata,

360
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:32,642
why don't you do the next surgery?

361
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:35,854
- What?
- Don't worry. I'll be assisting.

362
00:22:36,438 --> 00:22:38,315
Come on, that's ridiculous.

363
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:40,567
You're already familiar
with the procedure,

364
00:22:40,650 --> 00:22:44,237
since you saw what I did on Kanabun
when you removed her implant.

365
00:22:44,321 --> 00:22:45,489
It's not the same.

366
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:47,616
Putting them in
is easier than taking them out.

367
00:22:49,284 --> 00:22:53,121
A plastic surgeon actively practicing

368
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:56,708
should be able to do this procedure
with their eyes closed.

369
00:23:06,718 --> 00:23:07,719
Got him.

370
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:10,222
- Nice throw.
- Oh shit.

371
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:14,101
KILLER PSYCHO DOCTOR SENTENCED TO DEATH

372
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:18,271
Damn, that's cold.

373
00:23:19,147 --> 00:23:20,732
<i>Right, let's get started.</i>

374
00:23:29,783 --> 00:23:30,951
Numata's operating?

375
00:23:31,034 --> 00:23:33,328
A breast augmentation.

376
00:23:34,413 --> 00:23:35,664
Can you believe it?

377
00:23:36,373 --> 00:23:38,875
All right, now make an incision
along the marker.

378
00:23:38,959 --> 00:23:40,001
Yes, I know.

379
00:23:45,006 --> 00:23:46,967
- Two-pronged retractor, please.
- Here.

380
00:23:56,435 --> 00:23:58,437
- Insertion sleeve, please.
- Yes.

381
00:24:13,076 --> 00:24:14,286
Dr. Numata?

382
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:19,791
Yes, sorry.

383
00:24:22,461 --> 00:24:23,587
- Here.
- Okay.

384
00:24:53,950 --> 00:24:57,370
I'll finish everything else up.
You complete the medical paperwork.

385
00:24:57,454 --> 00:24:58,288
Okay.

386
00:24:58,371 --> 00:25:01,166
Make sure you're thorough.
Include as much detail as possible.

387
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:07,130
I'm very pleased.
You're just as good as they said you were.

388
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:29,694
PARTNER MODEL AGENCIES

389
00:25:33,907 --> 00:25:37,452
NATURÉ

390
00:25:39,120 --> 00:25:41,498
KANA KOKUBUN

391
00:25:41,581 --> 00:25:44,084
MALIGNANT TUMOR FINDINGS

392
00:25:45,669 --> 00:25:47,420
ENTER PASSWORD

393
00:25:48,338 --> 00:25:49,256
Mm.

394
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:56,263
- Ms. Miwa?
- Yes?

395
00:25:56,346 --> 00:25:59,516
I'm trying to complete my charts,
but do you know the password?

396
00:25:59,599 --> 00:26:02,769
Uh, sorry, only the doctors know that.

397
00:26:02,852 --> 00:26:04,187
- Oh, okay.
- Yeah.

398
00:26:17,701 --> 00:26:18,702
Thank you.

399
00:26:22,122 --> 00:26:23,915
Make room. Out of the way, please.

400
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,333
Thank you so much.

401
00:26:26,042 --> 00:26:28,587
Stand aside, please.
Let us pass. Coming through.

402
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:31,172
Come on, let's go.

403
00:26:31,256 --> 00:26:33,717
Ms. Tanaka!
Ms. Tanaka! Phone call for you.

404
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:35,594
It sounds like an emergency.

405
00:26:35,677 --> 00:26:37,804
Can I get your autograph, please?

406
00:26:38,305 --> 00:26:40,557
Please, just one selfie? Please!

407
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:44,227
Don't scare me like that!
I thought something had happened to Dad.

408
00:26:44,311 --> 00:26:47,230
<i>I had to.</i>
<i>You wouldn't have picked up otherwise.</i>

409
00:26:47,314 --> 00:26:49,649
<i>Besides, your dad isn't doing well.</i>

410
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:53,153
<i>I need you to come back to run the shop.</i>
<i>It's too much for me.</i>

411
00:26:53,236 --> 00:26:55,530
What, do you want me
to drop out of school? Is that it?

412
00:26:55,614 --> 00:26:57,115
<i>Don't be like that.</i>

413
00:26:57,699 --> 00:27:01,244
<i>People like us can't just climb the ranks.</i>
<i>Not in this world.</i>

414
00:27:01,745 --> 00:27:04,080
<i>You can't keep living in a fantasy.</i>

415
00:27:04,164 --> 00:27:05,582
I can do it!

416
00:27:06,791 --> 00:27:10,545
Just please let me try.

417
00:27:10,629 --> 00:27:11,546
Please.

418
00:27:12,047 --> 00:27:13,131
<i>Yoshiko…</i>

419
00:27:13,214 --> 00:27:15,634
We need all participants
to head to the main hall now.

420
00:27:15,717 --> 00:27:17,260
- <i>Yoshiko!</i>
- Yes!

421
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:23,224
<i>An outing?</i>

422
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:24,267
Yes.

423
00:27:24,351 --> 00:27:27,187
The whole staff
goes out together once a month.

424
00:27:27,270 --> 00:27:29,814
The director wanted to make sure
you were invited.

425
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:32,233
- Oh, that's not really my thing--
- Come on!

426
00:27:32,317 --> 00:27:34,819
It's a chance
for us to get to know each other.

427
00:27:35,487 --> 00:27:36,488
Ah.

428
00:27:36,988 --> 00:27:38,031
Okay, I'll check it out.

429
00:27:38,114 --> 00:27:39,866
Fantastic.

430
00:27:40,367 --> 00:27:43,286
Ah, just one more thing from the director.

431
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:46,289
It's really important
nobody recognizes you.

432
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:48,124
The backlash, you know?

433
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:50,460
Mm. For sure.

434
00:27:50,543 --> 00:27:51,586
I'll do that.

435
00:27:54,714 --> 00:27:57,342
- Wow, is that another new bag?
- Mm-hmm.

436
00:27:57,425 --> 00:27:58,718
Wow, that's so cute.

437
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:00,470
How many do you have?

438
00:28:00,553 --> 00:28:02,222
Hm. It's a secret.

439
00:28:06,643 --> 00:28:07,727
KABUKICHO ICHIBANGAI

440
00:28:07,811 --> 00:28:09,771
- Customers!
- Welcome.

441
00:28:16,486 --> 00:28:17,362
Hey.

442
00:28:22,992 --> 00:28:24,619
Welcome. First time?

443
00:28:24,703 --> 00:28:26,121
Didn't see this coming.

444
00:28:27,288 --> 00:28:29,749
VOICE ACTOR AUDITIONS

445
00:28:48,935 --> 00:28:51,104
Next up, Mashiro Himenoki,

446
00:28:51,187 --> 00:28:53,523
a third-year student
in the voice acting department.

447
00:29:10,498 --> 00:29:11,624
Oh, thank you.

448
00:29:14,085 --> 00:29:15,128
Excuse me.

449
00:29:20,925 --> 00:29:22,051
I'm Ryuga.

450
00:29:25,263 --> 00:29:26,097
May I?

451
00:29:30,226 --> 00:29:31,561
Are you recovering?

452
00:29:32,604 --> 00:29:35,315
Oh. Yeah, actually.

453
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:37,650
I just finished healing my nose.

454
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:39,903
Oh.

455
00:29:40,403 --> 00:29:42,655
I see.

456
00:29:43,323 --> 00:29:45,450
Does everyone who works here
get work done?

457
00:29:45,533 --> 00:29:47,535
I don't think
there's anyone left who hasn't.

458
00:29:47,619 --> 00:29:49,704
You have to keep up to survive.

459
00:29:49,788 --> 00:29:51,372
- Keep up?
- Mm.

460
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:53,291
Oh, wait. Are you new there?

461
00:29:53,374 --> 00:29:56,252
You don't know
our club is partnered with Tohyama?

462
00:29:56,753 --> 00:29:59,339
Oh. Right. Of course.
Yeah, that makes sense.

463
00:30:00,590 --> 00:30:04,135
You can't imagine the number of customers
we've referred to you guys.

464
00:30:04,219 --> 00:30:07,138
I was able to get my nose done
at a 50% discount.

465
00:30:08,181 --> 00:30:10,642
Oh.

466
00:30:12,894 --> 00:30:16,272
Hey. You can't drink alcohol.
Aren't you recovering?

467
00:30:16,356 --> 00:30:18,107
- Oh.
- Isn't that bad for you?

468
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:19,484
The alcohol disinfects.

469
00:30:27,826 --> 00:30:30,370
You can go ahead
and introduce yourself now.

470
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:35,250
Uh…

471
00:30:39,212 --> 00:30:41,422
Mm… Uh…

472
00:30:42,382 --> 00:30:43,341
Um…

473
00:30:43,925 --> 00:30:44,926
Uh…

474
00:30:45,677 --> 00:30:46,886
I'm going to…

475
00:30:50,473 --> 00:30:51,641
read this letter to my family.

476
00:30:51,724 --> 00:30:53,434
Your family?

477
00:30:54,185 --> 00:30:55,270
Because, well,

478
00:30:56,312 --> 00:30:58,439
I think that true voice acting…

479
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:02,735
relies on reading.

480
00:31:20,503 --> 00:31:21,671
"Dear Dad."

481
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:24,132
Mm.

482
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:26,926
"Thank you."

483
00:31:30,889 --> 00:31:32,056
"Dear Mom."

484
00:31:33,975 --> 00:31:34,851
"Thank you."

485
00:31:35,351 --> 00:31:37,937
"Thank you for raising me, even though

486
00:31:38,646 --> 00:31:40,690
I'm not anything special."

487
00:31:42,692 --> 00:31:43,651
"But…"

488
00:31:45,820 --> 00:31:46,946
"…I still…

489
00:31:49,324 --> 00:31:51,242
want to say to both of you…

490
00:31:54,287 --> 00:31:56,331
that the time has come to say goodbye."

491
00:31:57,332 --> 00:32:00,710
Welcome, partners
of the Tohyama Clinic Group.

492
00:32:00,793 --> 00:32:02,003
- The Hand of God!
- Yeah!

493
00:32:02,086 --> 00:32:04,088
Congrats! Their highest quarter yet!

494
00:32:04,172 --> 00:32:06,299
"Not to sound overly dramatic…"

495
00:32:10,261 --> 00:32:11,262
"…but I've…

496
00:32:13,306 --> 00:32:15,224
become someone totally new."

497
00:32:19,187 --> 00:32:20,563
"I'm no longer

498
00:32:20,647 --> 00:32:22,857
the sad little girl you once knew."

499
00:32:24,776 --> 00:32:25,902
"And I'm

500
00:32:27,236 --> 00:32:30,949
a better, stronger, braver person,
no longer hiding away!"

501
00:32:31,032 --> 00:32:32,700
Let's have the best night ever!

502
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:34,994
- Let's go!
- Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!

503
00:32:35,078 --> 00:32:38,373
- Yeah! Kings! Queens!
- Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

504
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:39,666
"I have been reborn

505
00:32:40,166 --> 00:32:41,584
into a wonderful…

506
00:32:43,753 --> 00:32:46,089
dazzling, beautiful, amazing new world!"

507
00:32:51,928 --> 00:32:52,929
"And I have…

508
00:32:58,601 --> 00:33:01,229
decided that this is the world
I'll live in."

509
00:33:03,940 --> 00:33:05,149
"Mom and Dad…"

510
00:33:07,735 --> 00:33:08,903
"…just know…

511
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:12,615
that it breaks my heart…"

512
00:33:13,908 --> 00:33:15,785
"…to leave you behind. I'm sorry."

513
00:33:20,415 --> 00:33:21,374
"But

514
00:33:23,209 --> 00:33:25,044
it is here on this stage…

515
00:33:27,213 --> 00:33:29,757
that I shall now give you
this final goodbye."

516
00:33:32,677 --> 00:33:35,430
"I shall soar in the sky
like a butterfly!"

517
00:33:37,807 --> 00:33:39,851
"I shall fly off to this brand-new world,

518
00:33:39,934 --> 00:33:41,561
so beautiful and exciting."

519
00:33:46,941 --> 00:33:48,234
"So farewell."

520
00:33:51,029 --> 00:33:52,030
"I love you."

521
00:33:53,614 --> 00:33:55,033
"Goodbye…

522
00:33:57,785 --> 00:33:58,870
Mom and Dad."

523
00:34:01,706 --> 00:34:02,999
"Farewell

524
00:34:05,001 --> 00:34:06,335
to my old self."

525
00:34:52,048 --> 00:34:53,049
Numata?

526
00:34:54,801 --> 00:34:56,302
Hey, are you okay?

527
00:34:56,385 --> 00:34:57,512
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

528
00:34:58,012 --> 00:34:59,222
Stop. You're drunk.

529
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:02,391
- Why are you even here?
- You haven't answered your phone or texts.

530
00:35:02,475 --> 00:35:04,644
You're getting it all over me!

531
00:35:04,727 --> 00:35:07,730
- Okay, you're all right.
- I'm sorry. I'm fine, I swear.

532
00:35:07,814 --> 00:35:09,023
- Leave me alone.
- No way.

533
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:10,566
- I'm not leaving you.
- Bye-bye!

534
00:35:10,650 --> 00:35:13,194
- What the hell? Come on.
- Get your hands off me.

535
00:35:19,075 --> 00:35:21,953
So you're working for a plastic surgeon?

536
00:35:23,538 --> 00:35:26,541
Not gonna lie. I'm honestly surprised.

537
00:35:27,041 --> 00:35:27,875
Yeah, duh.

538
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:31,212
I still can't believe I'm doing it.

539
00:35:32,004 --> 00:35:34,257
They take advantage of our insecurities.

540
00:35:35,633 --> 00:35:39,262
And they make us think beauty is the only
thing that could possibly matter.

541
00:35:39,345 --> 00:35:40,513
Disgusting.

542
00:35:41,055 --> 00:35:42,098
I guess.

543
00:35:42,181 --> 00:35:45,935
Still, sounds like it's the fastest way
to get your dad out of hot water

544
00:35:46,018 --> 00:35:48,020
and fix his money troubles.

545
00:35:48,855 --> 00:35:52,984
Don't you guys get paid
so much more than a regular doctor?

546
00:35:54,819 --> 00:35:57,780
Come on. Cut yourself some slack.

547
00:35:58,322 --> 00:36:01,242
You can always come back
once you've figured things out.

548
00:36:05,204 --> 00:36:07,248
Look, what I mean is,

549
00:36:08,708 --> 00:36:09,792
I'll be there for ya.

550
00:36:09,876 --> 00:36:13,254
If you ever need to vent, you call me.

551
00:36:13,337 --> 00:36:15,339
We'll get a drink.

552
00:36:31,105 --> 00:36:32,148
"Total Beauty?"

553
00:36:32,231 --> 00:36:36,068
Yes. We have a patient on the books today
for this package.

554
00:36:36,569 --> 00:36:39,614
The director asked me to make sure
that you had the necessary information.

555
00:36:40,114 --> 00:36:41,741
A full-body makeover?

556
00:36:41,824 --> 00:36:46,329
Yes, the patient leaves everything
up to the director, from head to toe.

557
00:36:47,079 --> 00:36:49,582
It's the most deluxe treatment package
we offer here.

558
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:54,795
Come in.

559
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:57,006
Excuse me.

560
00:36:57,506 --> 00:37:00,009
Ms. Sakashita is here for her appointment.

561
00:37:03,429 --> 00:37:04,472
Oh, hello.

562
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:05,890
It's lovely to meet you.

563
00:37:11,312 --> 00:37:14,690
Thank you for seeing me.
It's an honor to be here.

564
00:37:15,691 --> 00:37:19,362
<i>We shall now announce our five finalists.</i>

565
00:37:19,445 --> 00:37:20,404
First,

566
00:37:20,905 --> 00:37:21,989
Hinano Tachibana.

567
00:37:22,990 --> 00:37:24,116
Yes!

568
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,077
Wow!

569
00:37:26,160 --> 00:37:27,703
- Yurina Toyama.
- Yes!

570
00:37:27,787 --> 00:37:28,871
Great.

571
00:37:28,955 --> 00:37:30,998
- Sakura Shinomiya.
- Yes.

572
00:37:31,499 --> 00:37:33,292
- Saki Kashima.
- Yes.

573
00:37:33,793 --> 00:37:34,794
And lastly,

574
00:37:36,045 --> 00:37:37,213
Mashiro Himenoki.

575
00:37:40,841 --> 00:37:41,926
Tanaka.

576
00:37:44,595 --> 00:37:46,305
Oh. Y… Yes.

577
00:37:46,389 --> 00:37:50,059
Did you forget your own stage name?

578
00:37:50,142 --> 00:37:51,018
Sorry.

579
00:37:51,519 --> 00:37:55,231
Ms. Hiiragi spoke very highly
of your audition.

580
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:56,691
What?

581
00:37:57,316 --> 00:37:58,609
- She did?
- That's right.

582
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:02,154
In the final round, they'll be scoring
your singing and dancing abilities,

583
00:38:02,238 --> 00:38:03,823
so make sure you all practice.

584
00:38:03,906 --> 00:38:04,824
Yes.

585
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:10,621
All right,
I'm starting to paint a picture.

586
00:38:11,205 --> 00:38:13,541
Now, regarding your budget,

587
00:38:14,166 --> 00:38:16,502
Altogether, it looks like your package

588
00:38:16,585 --> 00:38:19,839
will cost at minimum… this amount.

589
00:38:19,922 --> 00:38:21,549
5 TO 7.5 MILLION

590
00:38:22,925 --> 00:38:26,429
- No problem. I trust you, Doctor.
- I'm glad to hear it.

591
00:38:27,013 --> 00:38:29,348
Well, we'll take a few photos
and draw a little blood.

592
00:38:29,432 --> 00:38:30,558
Okay.

593
00:38:30,641 --> 00:38:33,936
- Show her to the changing room.
- Of course. Right this way.

594
00:38:44,947 --> 00:38:46,782
- Right in there.
- Okay.

595
00:38:51,871 --> 00:38:55,082
- You can take a seat.
- Oh. Yes, of course.

596
00:38:59,337 --> 00:39:03,174
Sorry. I'm just a little nervous
since this morning.

597
00:39:03,799 --> 00:39:05,468
I even forgot

598
00:39:06,469 --> 00:39:08,012
to take my pills.

599
00:39:10,514 --> 00:39:12,558
I'm so forgetful these days.

600
00:39:17,104 --> 00:39:19,106
OPSO ORAL SOLUTION 5 MG

601
00:39:23,486 --> 00:39:24,612
Excuse me.

602
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:36,040
- Morphine?
- Yes.

603
00:39:36,540 --> 00:39:38,417
I saw her take the pills myself.

604
00:39:38,501 --> 00:39:42,254
I guess she has a serious condition
she hasn't told us about.

605
00:39:42,338 --> 00:39:44,590
She nearly collapsed outside
the other day.

606
00:39:46,300 --> 00:39:49,261
Besides, I don't think her body
is strong enough to handle surgery.

607
00:39:49,804 --> 00:39:51,222
<i>I understand.</i>

608
00:39:51,305 --> 00:39:54,475
I'll decide if she's a good candidate
once her blood work is in.

609
00:39:55,184 --> 00:39:58,687
Okay.

610
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:03,317
- One minute.
- Of course.

611
00:40:05,778 --> 00:40:07,029
Morning, Dad. Can I help you?

612
00:40:07,113 --> 00:40:09,073
<i>I'm sorry to bother you at work.</i>

613
00:40:09,573 --> 00:40:13,536
<i>It's just that, uh,</i>
<i>I heard a rather strange rumor.</i>

614
00:40:13,619 --> 00:40:15,538
I wanted to double-check it with you.

615
00:40:16,414 --> 00:40:20,334
- What rumor?
- <i>I'm not saying that it's true…</i>

616
00:40:20,918 --> 00:40:25,965
Uh, there's talk that the Tohyama director
made a critical medical error,

617
00:40:26,674 --> 00:40:28,300
and that a lot of clients, uh,

618
00:40:28,384 --> 00:40:30,010
are leaving for other clinics.

619
00:40:32,721 --> 00:40:34,807
Oh, you can't be serious. Come on, Dad.

620
00:40:34,890 --> 00:40:37,560
<i>Don't tell me you believe those lies.</i>

621
00:40:38,060 --> 00:40:40,604
Why don't you talk to our accountant?

622
00:40:40,688 --> 00:40:43,607
We're making even more money now
than when you were running the show.

623
00:40:43,691 --> 00:40:46,318
That's what I thought.

624
00:40:46,402 --> 00:40:50,739
It's just a silly rumor. You know people
will say anything to try to drag me down.

625
00:40:50,823 --> 00:40:52,116
That's all there is to it.

626
00:40:52,867 --> 00:40:54,493
I have to get back to work.

627
00:40:54,577 --> 00:40:55,661
However, that being said,

628
00:40:57,037 --> 00:40:59,790
the fact that you can't
nip these rumors in the bud,

629
00:41:00,541 --> 00:41:02,209
doesn't that mean you're losing your cred?

630
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:09,216
Oh, don't be ridiculous, Dad.

631
00:41:09,300 --> 00:41:11,760
<i>Our sales are great.</i>
<i>We're not losing anything.</i>

632
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:16,515
I've still got my reputation
as The Hand of God.

633
00:41:17,516 --> 00:41:18,476
Don't worry.

634
00:41:19,351 --> 00:41:20,644
That's good.

635
00:41:21,604 --> 00:41:24,690
Well, I'm glad
I got to hear it from you directly.

636
00:41:25,274 --> 00:41:27,318
Mm. Yeah.

637
00:42:11,612 --> 00:42:12,947
Dr. Tohyama?

638
00:42:15,950 --> 00:42:18,786
Oh. I'm so sorry.

639
00:42:18,869 --> 00:42:22,164
This question is from
a woman in her seventies.

640
00:42:22,248 --> 00:42:25,376
She'd like to know if there's an age limit
for plastic surgery.

641
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:28,879
Well, it depends on the procedure itself.

642
00:42:29,463 --> 00:42:34,635
However, I do think that any procedure
can be conducted safely on elderly people.

643
00:42:35,135 --> 00:42:38,013
Doctor, are you all right?
You seem a little off today.

644
00:42:39,306 --> 00:42:42,518
That's because you haven't
asked me to dinner today, Hamaguchi.

645
00:42:42,601 --> 00:42:46,146
Hey, that's not fair.
You never come when I do ask.

646
00:42:47,982 --> 00:42:49,775
But for real, are you okay?

647
00:42:49,858 --> 00:42:51,694
I'm absolutely fine.

648
00:42:52,194 --> 00:42:53,821
- Okay.
- Wait.

649
00:42:55,573 --> 00:42:57,575
- I was wondering…
- Yes?

650
00:42:58,158 --> 00:43:02,329
You once said that you'd be interested
in doing a documentary on the clinic?

651
00:43:02,413 --> 00:43:05,833
Oh, yeah, I'd love that.
An inside look on plastic surgery.

652
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:09,670
A documentary that shows patients and
doctors as their most authentic selves.

653
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:12,131
Mm. So…

654
00:43:14,466 --> 00:43:16,343
I might have an angle for you.

655
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:18,679
Yeah, yeah, that's right.

656
00:43:19,805 --> 00:43:21,724
Opso. Five milligrams.

657
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:23,350
Oh, I see.

658
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:27,313
Uh, if they're on Opso
and they're suffering hair loss,

659
00:43:27,396 --> 00:43:30,274
then that definitely points to cancer.

660
00:43:30,941 --> 00:43:34,653
And if we factor in their advanced age,
surgery would be a huge strain,

661
00:43:34,737 --> 00:43:37,948
so I imagine
that they're now in palliative care.

662
00:43:38,032 --> 00:43:39,241
That's what I thought.

663
00:43:40,576 --> 00:43:41,493
Yeah.

664
00:43:51,420 --> 00:43:52,379
Takeru.

665
00:43:53,839 --> 00:43:54,923
What are you doing?

666
00:43:56,008 --> 00:43:59,178
Well, you're the one
who said smiling makes you feel happier.

667
00:43:59,845 --> 00:44:01,096
- Huh?
- Yeah, I Googled it.

668
00:44:01,180 --> 00:44:02,806
Apparently, there's some truth to it.

669
00:44:04,058 --> 00:44:07,519
Just lifting the corners of your mouth
can improve your friendships.

670
00:44:08,020 --> 00:44:12,149
So, you're just gonna be smiling 24-7?

671
00:44:13,776 --> 00:44:14,735
You know,

672
00:44:15,235 --> 00:44:16,862
I'm thinking about eyelid surgery.

673
00:44:18,489 --> 00:44:21,033
- What?
- I think it would look good on me.

674
00:44:53,315 --> 00:44:55,526
Oh! Dr. Tohyama.

675
00:44:55,609 --> 00:44:58,112
- I'm sorry to be bothering you this late.
- It's fine.

676
00:44:58,737 --> 00:45:01,407
I just wanted to discuss something.

677
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:05,911
- Oh?
- This is Mr. Inoue, our legal advisor.

678
00:45:10,124 --> 00:45:13,085
- Won't you come in?
- Thank you so much.

679
00:45:15,087 --> 00:45:16,255
Yes, thank you.

680
00:45:26,098 --> 00:45:27,558
FILMING FOR A TV PROGRAM BEGINS TODAY

681
00:45:27,641 --> 00:45:28,767
What's going on here?

682
00:45:35,149 --> 00:45:36,859
Watch those cables.

683
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:39,528
We need to get this lighting set up.

684
00:45:40,738 --> 00:45:42,406
They're filming one of our clients

685
00:45:42,489 --> 00:45:44,825
for a Total Beauty documentary.

686
00:45:46,535 --> 00:45:48,245
A Total Beauty client?

687
00:45:50,414 --> 00:45:51,707
No, it can't be…

688
00:45:54,084 --> 00:45:55,335
Hey, what are you doing?

689
00:45:55,419 --> 00:45:57,504
I'm sorry. I don't have time right now.

690
00:45:58,297 --> 00:46:01,925
You said you'd wait for Ms.
Sakashita's test results before deciding.

691
00:46:02,009 --> 00:46:03,010
What were they?

692
00:46:03,927 --> 00:46:06,972
It doesn't matter. I already know.
She has terminal cancer.

693
00:46:11,685 --> 00:46:12,811
And if she does?

694
00:46:12,895 --> 00:46:16,398
You know what will happen if you
operate on someone in that condition.

695
00:46:16,482 --> 00:46:18,400
And now you're filming her?
What are you thinking?

696
00:46:18,484 --> 00:46:21,528
- Takashina, her consent form.
- What?

697
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:25,032
She told us herself directly
about her cancer diagnosis.

698
00:46:25,115 --> 00:46:27,743
She still agreed to both the surgery
and the documentary.

699
00:46:27,826 --> 00:46:29,369
I ACCEPT THE OUTCOME, WHATEVER IT MAY BE

700
00:46:29,453 --> 00:46:31,705
So you're going to exploit her
as a publicity stunt?

701
00:46:31,789 --> 00:46:36,418
Don't be so dramatic, Dr. Numata.
She has consented to be filmed.

702
00:46:36,502 --> 00:46:39,922
They won't film any surgery that may
require general anesthesia, so drop it.

703
00:46:40,547 --> 00:46:42,800
So, you're fine
just giving her whatever she asks for?

704
00:46:42,883 --> 00:46:46,345
If she says she wants to die, you'll just
kill her? Have you lost your damn mind?

705
00:46:47,054 --> 00:46:48,222
Hm.

706
00:46:48,305 --> 00:46:50,557
Someone who doesn't have much time left

707
00:46:50,641 --> 00:46:53,352
is asking for one last chance
to be beautiful!

708
00:46:54,436 --> 00:46:56,605
My duty is to help people like her.

709
00:46:57,898 --> 00:47:00,651
Life isn't just quantity.
It's also quality.

710
00:47:01,443 --> 00:47:03,320
There are ways to help
besides chemotherapy.

711
00:47:06,073 --> 00:47:07,115
I'm not cut out for this.

712
00:47:07,199 --> 00:47:08,659
Yeah, and don't I know it.

713
00:47:10,035 --> 00:47:12,162
I was hoping you'd rise to the occasion.

714
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:18,085
By all means, quit if you'd like.

715
00:47:18,585 --> 00:47:20,045
Of course,

716
00:47:21,588 --> 00:47:24,466
you will regain all your debt
if you do that.

717
00:47:51,118 --> 00:47:52,119
How was that?

718
00:47:54,705 --> 00:47:56,248
That was amazing!

719
00:47:56,331 --> 00:47:57,207
- Yay!
- Yay!

720
00:47:57,291 --> 00:47:59,793
Thank you!

721
00:47:59,877 --> 00:48:01,795
That was so good, Tanaka!

722
00:48:01,879 --> 00:48:03,088
Oh, Mr. Kudo.

723
00:48:04,047 --> 00:48:05,215
What is it?

724
00:48:06,383 --> 00:48:07,426
Well…

725
00:48:09,177 --> 00:48:10,679
Ms. Tanaka, we need to talk.

726
00:48:12,222 --> 00:48:13,056
Uh…

727
00:48:15,559 --> 00:48:18,020
You're gonna blow the whistle on Tohyama?

728
00:48:18,562 --> 00:48:19,897
How are you gonna do that?

729
00:48:20,480 --> 00:48:24,568
I looked at Kanabun's medical
records. There were signs of a tumor.

730
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:29,406
Which means the director already knew
about the tumor when she operated on her.

731
00:48:29,907 --> 00:48:32,409
I have full access
to these records. It's proof.

732
00:48:32,492 --> 00:48:35,037
So it'd be like an anonymous leak?

733
00:48:35,537 --> 00:48:37,372
That could get some traction.

734
00:48:37,456 --> 00:48:41,168
Also, I found a folder
for that modeling agency.

735
00:48:42,502 --> 00:48:44,087
I can expose that document too.

736
00:48:44,171 --> 00:48:47,382
Okay, then. We'll leak it on my page.

737
00:48:47,466 --> 00:48:49,968
Oh, but wait, what about all your debt?

738
00:48:50,052 --> 00:48:51,053
Oh, well,

739
00:48:51,887 --> 00:48:53,847
I'll figure that out.
Don't worry about it.

740
00:48:56,141 --> 00:48:57,768
- Dr. Hikita.
- Mm.

741
00:48:57,851 --> 00:48:59,061
- Hi.
- Hi.

742
00:49:00,312 --> 00:49:03,732
Uh… Hey, you know the files
containing the surgery data?

743
00:49:03,815 --> 00:49:07,027
- Yeah.
- Would you mind telling me the password?

744
00:49:08,153 --> 00:49:09,196
What?

745
00:49:10,238 --> 00:49:12,366
- Why would you need that?
- Oh.

746
00:49:12,449 --> 00:49:16,954
It's just that the director
wants me to study your previous surgeries.

747
00:49:17,037 --> 00:49:18,330
She never told me the password.

748
00:49:18,830 --> 00:49:20,415
Oh.

749
00:49:21,291 --> 00:49:23,043
So you decided to go through with it, huh?

750
00:49:25,545 --> 00:49:27,589
- Is it cool that I asked you?
- Yeah.

751
00:49:28,715 --> 00:49:30,467
- Forfeit?
- Mm.

752
00:49:30,550 --> 00:49:33,345
But I don't understand. Why would I quit?

753
00:49:33,428 --> 00:49:35,806
Well, it seems we've got an issue.

754
00:49:35,889 --> 00:49:38,225
- What? What kind of issue?
- Listen.

755
00:49:38,850 --> 00:49:41,478
Ms. Hiiragi received an anonymous message

756
00:49:41,561 --> 00:49:45,148
claiming you were sugar dating
to pay for your plastic surgery.

757
00:49:46,274 --> 00:49:49,319
Her manager called me immediately.
She's concerned.

758
00:49:49,403 --> 00:49:51,571
Agencies are uncomfortable
with that kind of thing.

759
00:49:51,655 --> 00:49:53,824
- But--
- I know. I know.

760
00:50:04,751 --> 00:50:08,588
I know this is hard.
Listen. Here's my advice.

761
00:50:10,799 --> 00:50:13,552
If you drop out,
it's not an admission of guilt.

762
00:50:14,094 --> 00:50:16,555
<i>I know it's hard.</i>
<i>You can try out again next time.</i>

763
00:50:16,638 --> 00:50:17,639
I won't do it!

764
00:50:17,723 --> 00:50:20,600
I won't. I'm not gonna drop out!

765
00:50:20,684 --> 00:50:22,853
<i>Please think about the school.</i>

766
00:50:23,353 --> 00:50:26,898
This agency collaboration could benefit us
so much. We need the audition to go well.

767
00:50:26,982 --> 00:50:28,817
If I fail at this, I'll have nothing left.

768
00:50:28,900 --> 00:50:30,861
If they find proof of your actions,

769
00:50:30,944 --> 00:50:34,156
you could jeopardize the chances
of any future students, and then what?

770
00:50:34,239 --> 00:50:35,449
You could ruin the--

771
00:50:36,825 --> 00:50:38,201
Is everything okay?

772
00:50:39,202 --> 00:50:41,121
Are you fighting about something?

773
00:50:42,372 --> 00:50:43,331
Hm.

774
00:50:50,255 --> 00:50:51,256
You did it.

775
00:50:55,677 --> 00:50:56,887
It was you, wasn't it?

776
00:51:05,145 --> 00:51:06,229
What do you mean?

777
00:51:08,690 --> 00:51:10,358
How… How…

778
00:51:10,942 --> 00:51:13,695
- How could you do that?
- Stop! Get off. Hey!

779
00:51:13,779 --> 00:51:15,572
- How could you do this to me?
- Ow!

780
00:51:15,655 --> 00:51:17,032
Hey, girls, stop it!

781
00:51:17,115 --> 00:51:18,325
Why? How could you?!

782
00:51:23,955 --> 00:51:25,582
PARTNER MODEL AGENCIES

783
00:51:27,375 --> 00:51:28,794
USER ACCESSING PROTECTED FILE
HIKITA

784
00:51:28,877 --> 00:51:29,920
Mr. Hikita?

785
00:51:32,130 --> 00:51:33,465
Takashina!

786
00:51:33,548 --> 00:51:34,549
Yes?

787
00:51:34,633 --> 00:51:37,803
- It was you! No one else knew about it!
- Get off!

788
00:51:37,886 --> 00:51:40,097
I know it was you! What is wrong with you?

789
00:51:40,180 --> 00:51:42,641
- Knock it off!
- You're crazy. Let me go!

790
00:52:16,925 --> 00:52:18,218
You free?

791
00:52:18,301 --> 00:52:19,761
- I'm free.
- Excuse me!

792
00:52:19,845 --> 00:52:22,389
Hey! Numata, watch where you're going.

793
00:52:33,859 --> 00:52:36,444
- Knock it off! Break it up already!
- Get off of me!

794
00:52:36,528 --> 00:52:38,488
You scratched me!

795
00:52:38,572 --> 00:52:40,073
You can go to hell!

796
00:52:40,657 --> 00:52:43,076
I never want to see you again!

797
00:52:43,160 --> 00:52:45,662
- You just thought I'd beat you!
- You beat me?

798
00:52:46,788 --> 00:52:48,290
You're delusional!

799
00:52:48,373 --> 00:52:49,916
Stop!

800
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:51,960
Quiet!

801
00:52:56,840 --> 00:52:58,300
You'd lose.

802
00:53:00,385 --> 00:53:02,971
You can't even dance.

803
00:53:04,264 --> 00:53:10,145
It'd be way too easy to beat you!

804
00:53:42,302 --> 00:53:44,346
<i>Are you struggling with something?</i>

805
00:53:46,056 --> 00:53:47,724
<i>Your new self</i>

806
00:53:48,516 --> 00:53:49,851
<i>begins right here.</i>

807
00:53:51,269 --> 00:53:53,730
<i>Turn that dream into reality.</i>

808
00:53:54,814 --> 00:53:56,983
<i>You can be reborn.</i>

809
00:53:58,068 --> 00:53:59,444
<i>The Hand of God</i>

810
00:53:59,945 --> 00:54:01,238
<i>can change you.</i>

811
00:54:03,406 --> 00:54:04,908
<i>Do it for yourself.</i>

812
00:54:06,785 --> 00:54:09,913
<i>Are you satisfied</i>
<i>with who you are right now?</i>

813
00:54:11,456 --> 00:54:12,791
<i>Everyone…</i>

814
00:54:14,626 --> 00:54:17,003
<i>deserves to be beautiful.</i>

815
00:54:19,172 --> 00:54:21,841
<i>Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic.</i>

816
00:54:29,641 --> 00:54:32,811
Who were you going to send these to?
A tabloid, I guess?

817
00:54:34,980 --> 00:54:36,940
All right.

818
00:54:37,023 --> 00:54:38,566
Let's cut the bullshit.

819
00:54:39,150 --> 00:54:42,946
First of all, Numata, stealing
confidential information is a felony.

820
00:54:43,613 --> 00:54:45,073
Punishable by jail.

821
00:54:47,951 --> 00:54:49,911
Are you even listening to me?

822
00:54:51,162 --> 00:54:52,872
Director, may I have a word?

823
00:54:52,956 --> 00:54:53,957
Not right now.

824
00:54:54,040 --> 00:54:56,584
It's important, Director Tohyama,
I assure you.

825
00:54:58,628 --> 00:55:00,797
It's okay. We can fix this.

826
00:55:00,880 --> 00:55:02,924
I promise. It's going to be okay.

827
00:55:03,008 --> 00:55:04,801
- Ms. Tanaka?
- Dr. Rin!

828
00:55:05,969 --> 00:55:07,470
Oh, Doctor, please!

829
00:55:07,554 --> 00:55:10,140
- Please tell me you can fix this!
- Ms. Tanaka, just calm down.

830
00:55:10,223 --> 00:55:11,975
- You have to do it!
- Prepare her for surgery.

831
00:55:12,058 --> 00:55:13,393
- Yes.
- Okay.

832
00:55:13,476 --> 00:55:15,437
- Fix me, please!
- Relax.

833
00:55:15,520 --> 00:55:16,813
It'll be okay.

834
00:55:16,896 --> 00:55:18,315
Okay, just breathe.

835
00:55:18,398 --> 00:55:21,776
Ms. Tanaka, I know you're in pain,
but please listen.

836
00:55:22,277 --> 00:55:25,196
I promise you I will fix your nose, okay?

837
00:55:25,280 --> 00:55:26,656
It'll be fine.

838
00:55:26,740 --> 00:55:28,199
But for that to happen,

839
00:55:28,700 --> 00:55:30,702
you'll need a very long recovery.

840
00:55:30,785 --> 00:55:32,162
No, please!

841
00:55:32,245 --> 00:55:34,789
I have the final round
of auditions next week.

842
00:55:34,873 --> 00:55:38,043
- You can try again next year.
- No it has to be this year!

843
00:55:38,126 --> 00:55:40,337
I won't get this chance again!

844
00:55:40,420 --> 00:55:41,379
Please!

845
00:55:41,463 --> 00:55:43,048
I have to win.

846
00:55:45,091 --> 00:55:46,343
Doctor…

847
00:55:50,638 --> 00:55:51,556
Director.

848
00:55:54,100 --> 00:55:56,144
You're really going to do this surgery?

849
00:55:59,856 --> 00:56:01,399
She wants to do this audition.

850
00:56:01,483 --> 00:56:05,403
She'll be swollen and bruised.
How can you in good conscience do this?

851
00:56:07,030 --> 00:56:10,700
You know what could happen if you put
a prosthesis in. She's at high-risk for--

852
00:56:10,784 --> 00:56:13,953
- Do you have a better plan?
- Yes, first repair the broken bone.

853
00:56:14,496 --> 00:56:16,247
Wait for it to heal.

854
00:56:18,166 --> 00:56:19,793
It's the medically responsible
thing to do.

855
00:56:22,003 --> 00:56:24,089
I can't do a procedure she doesn't want.

856
00:56:24,172 --> 00:56:25,590
Then let me do it.

857
00:56:31,346 --> 00:56:32,722
Can I go talk to her?

858
00:56:37,936 --> 00:56:39,104
Ms. Tanaka?

859
00:56:43,483 --> 00:56:44,984
Do you remember me?

860
00:56:47,904 --> 00:56:49,406
Katsushika Hospital.

861
00:56:54,077 --> 00:56:56,788
I remember you very well, Ms. Tanaka.

862
00:56:57,997 --> 00:56:59,791
And what your face looked like before.

863
00:57:07,841 --> 00:57:09,884
I used to work in the ER.

864
00:57:10,927 --> 00:57:15,473
So, as you can imagine,
I've worked on a lot of facial injuries.

865
00:57:15,557 --> 00:57:17,892
I will do my absolute best

866
00:57:19,227 --> 00:57:20,979
to help fix your injury.

867
00:57:25,733 --> 00:57:26,943
You have my word.

868
00:57:28,445 --> 00:57:29,779
So my recommendation

869
00:57:29,863 --> 00:57:33,074
is that we first restore your nose
to its original state.

870
00:57:35,452 --> 00:57:42,459
VIOLET EIKAEN

871
00:57:47,213 --> 00:57:49,215
TEMPORARILY CLOSED
FOR PERSONAL REASONS

872
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:12,989
Yoshi?

873
00:58:14,908 --> 00:58:16,075
Yoshi!

874
00:58:17,744 --> 00:58:20,497
You came back. I can't believe it!

875
00:58:21,372 --> 00:58:23,333
We got him through the worst of it,

876
00:58:23,958 --> 00:58:26,002
but he still hasn't
regained consciousness.

877
00:58:27,212 --> 00:58:29,422
I know he would have wanted you here,

878
00:58:29,923 --> 00:58:32,425
so I begged the doctor
to let me bring him home.

879
00:58:34,928 --> 00:58:36,429
Before the stroke,

880
00:58:36,513 --> 00:58:39,891
he was looking forward to teaching you
how to run the business.

881
00:58:40,475 --> 00:58:42,268
To spend time with you.

882
00:58:45,146 --> 00:58:46,147
Sweetie.

883
00:58:47,315 --> 00:58:48,733
She came back.

884
00:58:49,317 --> 00:58:51,277
Yoshiko is here, darling.

885
00:58:52,904 --> 00:58:54,739
So please get better soon.

886
00:58:54,822 --> 00:58:57,951
You have to show her the ropes
at the store.

887
00:59:00,245 --> 00:59:01,287
I'm sorry.

888
00:59:03,248 --> 00:59:04,082
Mom…

889
00:59:07,043 --> 00:59:08,169
I…

890
00:59:11,673 --> 00:59:14,259
I can't give up on my dream. Not yet.

891
00:59:15,009 --> 00:59:15,885
But…

892
00:59:17,887 --> 00:59:19,889
what's gonna happen to the store then?

893
00:59:46,499 --> 00:59:48,626
I'm not Yoshiko Tanaka now.

894
00:59:52,797 --> 00:59:55,425
I am Mashiro Himenoki. All right?

895
01:00:05,893 --> 01:00:07,061
I'm sorry.

896
01:00:11,858 --> 01:00:12,984
I have to…

897
01:00:16,654 --> 01:00:18,823
live the life I want in Tokyo.

898
01:00:28,249 --> 01:00:29,250
You can't.

899
01:00:31,502 --> 01:00:33,212
Please don't give me my old nose.

900
01:00:36,758 --> 01:00:37,925
Why not?

901
01:00:38,009 --> 01:00:41,262
- You can audition next year--
- It's not about the audition.

902
01:00:42,722 --> 01:00:43,931
I just can't.

903
01:00:46,643 --> 01:00:49,020
Please, I can't bear
to have that face again.

904
01:00:52,565 --> 01:00:54,108
If you do that…

905
01:00:57,570 --> 01:00:59,405
I will kill myself.

906
01:01:05,328 --> 01:01:06,913
The surgery…

907
01:01:09,791 --> 01:01:11,918
changed my life in the best way.

908
01:01:14,921 --> 01:01:17,882
I was finally able
to live to the fullest without fear.

909
01:01:23,805 --> 01:01:25,848
I want Dr. Rin to fix it.

910
01:01:29,894 --> 01:01:30,770
I…

911
01:01:34,190 --> 01:01:36,859
I won't let you do my surgery.

912
01:01:53,042 --> 01:01:56,921
Why don't we fit that new procedure
in once you have some time for recovery?

913
01:01:57,004 --> 01:01:58,131
Oh yes, please.

914
01:01:58,214 --> 01:02:00,508
Sounds good, Kotomi.
I'll see you next week.

915
01:02:00,591 --> 01:02:02,301
All right. See you next week.

916
01:02:10,810 --> 01:02:12,854
Oh, just to fill you in,

917
01:02:13,354 --> 01:02:16,649
Ms. Tanaka will be able
to attend her audition after all.

918
01:02:17,233 --> 01:02:19,026
I managed to get it postponed.

919
01:02:21,654 --> 01:02:23,322
Pays to have friends in high places.

920
01:02:25,491 --> 01:02:29,579
All I did was ask Kotomi
to give Ms. Tanaka another chance.

921
01:02:30,079 --> 01:02:32,707
The rest will be up to Ms. Tanaka.

922
01:02:34,667 --> 01:02:35,793
One other thing.

923
01:02:37,962 --> 01:02:39,630
If you wouldn't mind, Doctor,

924
01:02:40,131 --> 01:02:42,925
it would go a long way if you could
take that scowl off your face.

925
01:02:54,270 --> 01:02:56,522
It's the murderer's brother!
Where are you going?

926
01:02:56,606 --> 01:02:59,484
Hey, get back here!

927
01:02:59,567 --> 01:03:01,360
Hey! Answer us!

928
01:03:01,444 --> 01:03:04,113
You're running off
to go kill someone too. Is that it?

929
01:03:05,156 --> 01:03:06,908
Whoa. Why is he smiling?

930
01:03:06,991 --> 01:03:09,035
Yeah, weird. He's a total psycho!

931
01:03:11,078 --> 01:03:13,414
Oh damn, run! I can't get caught again!

932
01:03:20,922 --> 01:03:22,131
How you been?

933
01:03:31,432 --> 01:03:33,434
Okay, now let's get a close-up.

934
01:03:41,776 --> 01:03:43,110
Wow, look at her.

935
01:03:43,194 --> 01:03:45,488
Her skin's hanging off her bones.

936
01:03:45,571 --> 01:03:46,781
Think she'll be okay?

937
01:03:46,864 --> 01:03:49,700
She better not die halfway through.
The whole project would be scrapped.

938
01:03:49,784 --> 01:03:51,911
Come on. Don't joke around like that.

939
01:03:55,623 --> 01:03:57,542
Okay. That's all we need here.

940
01:03:58,042 --> 01:04:01,420
Great work. That's all we need
for pictures today, Ms. Yuriko.

941
01:04:01,504 --> 01:04:02,713
They'll do your interview next.

942
01:04:02,797 --> 01:04:04,131
- Go ahead and get changed.
- Okay.

943
01:04:09,387 --> 01:04:11,013
KANA KOKUBUN

944
01:04:12,640 --> 01:04:14,016
MALIGNANT TUMOR FINDINGS

945
01:04:16,435 --> 01:04:19,105
DELETE ALL FILES?

946
01:04:23,734 --> 01:04:25,152
DELETED
